$\begin{align}
\text{vertex's }r\text{-coordinate}&=\dfrac{(\goldD{2})+(\goldD{-13})}{2}
\\\\
&=-\blueD{\dfrac{11}{2}}
\end{align}$

Now we can find the vertex's $y$-coordinate by evaluating $h\left(\blueD{-\dfrac{11}{2}}\right)$:

$\begin{align}
h\left(\blueD{-\dfrac{11}{2}}\right)&=\left(\blueD{-\dfrac{11}{2}}\right)^2+11\left(-\blueD{\dfrac{11}{2}}\right)-26
\\\\
&=\dfrac{121}{4}-\dfrac{121}{2}-26
\\\\
&=-\dfrac{225}{4}
\end{align}$
